1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,779
An assistant that forgets you after every chat makes you repeat yourself.

2
00:00:05,779 --> 00:00:10,740
This video shows how AI memory lets an assistant remember stable facts about

3
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:15,640
each signed-in user, how to set it up, and how people clear what was saved.

4
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:23,416
Without memory, every chat starts from nothing.

5
00:00:23,416 --> 00:00:28,090
People repeat their name, their role, and how they like answers written.

6
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:34,060
With memory, an assistant keeps a few stable facts about each signed-in person,

7
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:36,210
and uses them in later chats.

8
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:38,376
Memory is private.

9
00:00:38,376 --> 00:00:43,390
The assistant only reads and changes the memory of the person it is talking to.

10
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:49,641
It is for lasting, non-sensitive facts, such as a preferred name, a role,

11
00:00:49,641 --> 00:00:51,520
or a preferred style.

12
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:55,350
Passwords, keys and card numbers are never saved.

13
00:00:59,550 --> 00:01:03,515
Memories are kept in a search index, so the assistant can find the

14
00:01:03,515 --> 00:01:05,002
right one by meaning.

15
00:01:05,002 --> 00:01:06,820
You create that index once.

16
00:01:07,570 --> 00:01:12,442
The site settings say which index holds the memories, and how many come

17
00:01:12,442 --> 00:01:14,150
back for each search.

18
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:17,732
Each profile decides whether to use memory.

19
00:01:17,732 --> 00:01:19,870
It is off until you turn it on.

20
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:22,191
People stay in control.

21
00:01:22,191 --> 00:01:27,390
They can ask the assistant what it remembers, and clear everything from their own profile.

22
00:01:31,627 --> 00:01:34,136
Memory needs a search index.

23
00:01:34,136 --> 00:01:37,677
Open Search, Indexes, and click Add index.

24
00:01:38,153 --> 00:01:41,324
Click Add on AI Memory for Elasticsearch.

25
00:01:41,324 --> 00:01:46,653
The type for Azure AI Search works the same way, when that feature is on.

26
00:01:47,109 --> 00:01:51,739
Enter an Index Name, and a Name, which is how the index is listed.

27
00:01:52,226 --> 00:01:54,363
Pick the Embedding deployment.

28
00:01:54,363 --> 00:01:59,052
It turns each memory into numbers that the search compares, and it cannot

29
00:01:59,052 --> 00:02:01,366
be changed once the index exists.

30
00:02:01,862 --> 00:02:04,479
The other fields can stay as they are.

31
00:02:04,479 --> 00:02:07,572
Click Save, and the index appears in the list.

32
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:16,150
Open Settings, Artificial Intelligence, and find the Memory section.

33
00:02:16,609 --> 00:02:18,341
Pick the Index profile.

34
00:02:18,341 --> 00:02:22,820
This one index holds the memories of every user, so avoid changing it

35
00:02:22,820 --> 00:02:27,119
once people use memory, or the saved memories are no longer found.

36
00:02:27,649 --> 00:02:33,189
Default top N is how many saved memories the assistant gets back when it searches.

37
00:02:33,926 --> 00:02:40,729
Under General, Enable preemptive memory retrieval looks up a person's memories before the model answers.

38
00:02:40,729 --> 00:02:44,626
Turn it off to keep the memory tools, but skip that step.

39
00:02:45,234 --> 00:02:49,636
Enable user memory turns memory on for chat interactions.

40
00:02:49,636 --> 00:02:50,824
Click Save.

41
00:02:55,037 --> 00:03:00,401
Open Artificial Intelligence, Profiles, and edit the profile of an assistant that people

42
00:03:00,401 --> 00:03:03,197
use every day, such as a support assistant.

43
00:03:03,653 --> 00:03:06,999
On the Knowledge tab, tick Enable user memory.

44
00:03:06,999 --> 00:03:11,953
Memory is off by default on every profile, so you choose where it fits.

45
00:03:12,449 --> 00:03:15,845
Use it for an internal assistant your staff rely on.

46
00:03:15,845 --> 00:03:18,772
Leave it off for a public website assistant:

47
00:03:18,772 --> 00:03:21,349
memory only works for signed-in users.

48
00:03:21,799 --> 00:03:22,919
Click Save.

49
00:03:22,919 --> 00:03:28,779
Profile templates have the same checkbox, so new profiles can start with memory on.

50
00:03:33,079 --> 00:03:34,233
Now try it.

51
00:03:34,233 --> 00:03:39,659
In the list of profiles, open Actions on the assistant and click New chat.

52
00:03:41,599 --> 00:03:44,460
Tell the assistant something worth keeping.

53
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:48,489
Here the user says to be called Sam, and to keep answers short.

54
00:03:48,955 --> 00:03:52,385
The assistant saves it as a memory, and answers.

55
00:03:52,850 --> 00:03:54,135
Click New Chat.

56
00:03:54,135 --> 00:03:59,520
This chat has no history, but the assistant looks up the memory before it answers.

57
00:04:00,014 --> 00:04:01,508
Ask what it remembers.

58
00:04:01,508 --> 00:04:05,564
The assistant looks up its memories, and answers with the name that it

59
00:04:05,564 --> 00:04:07,164
saved in the other chat.

60
00:04:11,391 --> 00:04:14,192
People can clear what the assistant saved.

61
00:04:14,192 --> 00:04:17,751
Open the user menu at the top right, and click Profile.

62
00:04:18,235 --> 00:04:22,745
The AI Memory section shows a Danger zone when memories are saved.

63
00:04:23,204 --> 00:04:26,771
Click Clear saved AI memory, and confirm with Clear.

64
00:04:26,771 --> 00:04:32,184
Everything the assistant remembered about you is removed, and it cannot be undone.

65
00:04:32,670 --> 00:04:36,404
The section now says that no saved AI memory was found.

66
00:04:36,404 --> 00:04:41,363
An administrator with the Clear AI memory for other users permission can do

67
00:04:41,363 --> 00:04:45,220
the same from Access Control, Users, by editing the user.

68
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:50,874
Staff assistants:

69
00:04:50,874 --> 00:04:56,120
they learn names, roles and preferred styles, so each answer starts closer to

70
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,890
what the person wants.

71
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:00,339
Specialist assistants:

72
00:05:00,339 --> 00:05:04,710
they keep track of the projects and topics a person works on most.

73
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:06,658
Fresh starts:

74
00:05:06,658 --> 00:05:12,400
people ask the assistant to forget one thing, or clear everything from their profile.

75
00:05:13,150 --> 00:05:14,584
Not for secrets:

76
00:05:14,584 --> 00:05:20,780
memory is for stable, non-sensitive facts, and public website assistants stay without it.

77
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:26,910
Create the memory index, choose it in the settings, and turn memory on

78
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:28,649
for the profiles that fit.

79
00:05:28,649 --> 00:05:32,507
Your assistants then remember people, and people stay in control.

80
00:05:32,507 --> 00:05:33,920
Thanks for watching.

